mly'"}]}]}]}]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["If the property name is known but ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"no worker advertises a satisfying\nvalue"}],", the scheduler's matching pass returns without doing anything.\nThe action stays ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Queued"}],". Nothing escalates, nothing times out, nothing is\nlogged above ",["$","code",null,{"children":"INFO"}],"."]}]]]}]]}]
30:["$","p",null,{"children":"That second case is not a bug so much as a consequence of how matching works\n(\"no worker matches yet\" is indistinguishable from \"no worker matches ever\"),\nbut its operational effect is a build that hangs with no diagnostic."}]
31:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"max_action_executing_timeout_s"}]," does not help, because it applies only to the\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"Executing"}]," state and the action never reaches it. The only thing that ever\nends the wait is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"client_action_timeout_s"}]," (default 60 s) noticing the client\nhas stopped listening, which produces a message about\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"#the-timeout-message-that-tells-you-nothing","children":"clients listening"}]," and says\nnothing about properties."]}]
